📅 Day 43 – Bootstrap Grid System

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on the Bootstrap Grid System and how it is used to create responsive layouts efficiently. The mentor explained how Bootstrap simplifies layout design using a 12-column grid structure.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Bootstrap Grid System
Bootstrap uses a 12-column layout system
Helps in creating responsive web pages
Layout is divided using:
container → Main wrapper
row → Horizontal group of columns
col → Individual columns
2️⃣ Grid Classes
col- → For extra small devices
col-sm- → Small devices
col-md- → Medium devices
col-lg- → Large devices
col-xl- → Extra large devices
3️⃣ Breakpoints

Bootstrap uses breakpoints to adjust layouts for different screen sizes:

Mobile
Tablet
Desktop

This ensures content adapts properly across devices.

